"source":"online_short.py",
"code":"import sys\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(d[0])\n    vals = d[1:n + 1]\n    a = list(map(int, vals))\n    qs = d[n + 1:]\n    last = 0\n    for k in (0, 2):\n        x = int(qs[k])\n        y = int(qs[k + 1])\n        lo = (x + last) % n\n        hi = (y + last) % n\n        if lo > hi:\n            lo, hi = hi, lo\n        seg = a[lo:hi + 1]\n        last = sum(seg)\n        print(last)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
"alt":"A short version of the encrypted-query program for six values and two range-sum lines. The answer to the first line is kept in last, and both numbers of the second line are decoded with it before its range is known. A plain slice sum stands in for the tree.",
